    "type": "question",
    "label": "43",
    "prompt": "How many people are in a room if there are 190 distinct pairings?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "20 people.\n\nSet $\\binom{n}{2}=190$ and take the positive solution.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the number of people. Each distinct pairing is an unordered selection of two people. $$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n}{2}&=190\\\\\\frac{n!}{2!(n-2)!}&=190\\\\\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}&=190\\\\n(n-1)&=380\\\\n^2-n-380&=0\\\\(n-20)(n+19)&=0.\\end{align*}$$ Since $n\\geq2$, $n=20$. There are 20 people.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 73
  },
